.TH env 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
env \- run a command in a modified environment, or show the environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B env
[\fB\-i\fR] [\fB\-a\fR] [\fIname\fB=\fIvalue\fR ...] [\fIcommand\fR [\fIargument\fR ...]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B env
sets each
.IB name = value
in the environment and then runs
.IR command .
With no
.IR command ,
it prints the resulting environment, one variable per line.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-i
Start from an empty environment rather than the current one.  A bare
.B \-
means the same.
.TP
.B \-a
The argument after
.I command
is
.IR "argv[0]" ,
so the program can be given a name other than its path.
.TP
.B \-\-
End of options.
.SH EXIT STATUS
127 if
.I command
was not found, 126 if it could not be run, otherwise whatever the
command returned.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# env
# env PAGER=cat man sed
# env -i sh
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR printenv (1),
.BR sh (1)
